WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.650
Diego had only just found his footing when
it gave out underneath him again.

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:10.269
Crashing to the ground, he threw both arms
over his head just in time to protect his

00:00:10.269 --> 00:00:14.510
skull from the rain of boulders that came
down past him.

00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:19.270
They grazed his arms and jarred painfully
against his muscles, but it was better than

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:21.890
having them hit him in the head.

00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:26.529
Without a moment to spare, Diego got straight
up to his feet and continued running back

00:00:26.529 --> 00:00:29.540
down the trail he had been trying to follow.

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:34.610
The ground shifted and lurched in all directions
under him, threatening to throw off his balance

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:36.050
at any moment.

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:40.840
Having lived in Chile his whole life, he had
gotten used to earthquakes, but he had never

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:43.410
been in the center of one like this.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:46.980
The problem was that the trail he had been
following to get up here was disappearing

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:51.500
fast as the dust swirled into the air and
boulders landed all around him.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.410
He just had to keep running in this direction
and hope for the best.

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:58.050
There weren't any other options.

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:01.350
But suddenly, he found himself running uphill.

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:04.900
Stumbling forwards, Diego tried desperately
to get his bearings.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:10.040
He had spent the previous three hours hiking
up the mountains, so how was it that now that

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:14.280
he had turned around and gone back, he was
still going uphill?

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:20.119
It was almost as if the ground was changing
shape beneath him as he ran.

00:01:20.119 --> 00:01:23.820
Dust filled his lungs as he tried to wipe
it away from his burning eyes.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:30.009
Yes, the ground was definitely going uphill,
but it felt almost as if it was lifting itself

00:01:30.009 --> 00:01:36.110
up beneath him, as if some tectonic plates
were grinding together, creating a new mountain

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:37.710
beneath his feet.

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:42.299
Diego lurched unsteadily and grabbed the nearest
rock to keep his balance, feeling the ground

00:01:42.299 --> 00:01:45.250
lifting higher and higher beneath him.

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:51.100
Then, all of a sudden, the cloud of dust broke,
and he was in fresh air rising ever higher

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:52.759
into the sky.

00:01:52.759 --> 00:01:57.770
The Andes mountains stabbed out of the clouds
all around him, cutting beautiful shapes across

00:01:57.770 --> 00:01:58.770
the horizon.

00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:02.390
He felt his own mountain steadily growing
taller than any of them.

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:07.180
He dropped down on all fours and clutched
at the ground in terror as he tried his best

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:11.329
to take in the shape of what he was now standing
upon.

00:02:11.329 --> 00:02:12.329
*

00:02:12.329 --> 00:02:15.540
How far would you go to prevent a cosmic-level
disaster?

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:19.620
It's one thing to save your friends and family
from an armed murderer; it's another thing

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:22.120
to fight for your country in a world war.

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:27.410
We can even just about imagine what it means
to fight for our planet, to save our species

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:31.400
from climate change, to save our world from
a meteorite.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:34.540
But what would a cosmic disaster look like?

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:41.790
A calamity so broad in scale that it surpasses
our ability to even perceive the threat.

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:46.069
We could point our most advanced telescope
into deep space and look straight down the

00:02:46.069 --> 00:02:49.379
middle of it, and never know it's even there.

00:02:49.379 --> 00:02:55.180
And if that threat was not simply to the survival
of humanity or planet Earth but to the survival

00:02:55.180 --> 00:03:00.959
of existence itself, how far would we go to
prevent it?

00:03:00.959 --> 00:03:07.379
What cruel and inhumane measures would you
take to have such a threat?

00:03:07.379 --> 00:03:11.740
How many people would you kill to save the
world?

00:03:11.740 --> 00:03:17.190
This debate is raging right now as you sit
here and watch this video, not among the Foundation

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:23.440
but between two SCPs so grand in scale and
so advanced in nature that the Foundation

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:30.200
has no option but to sit and listen as the
pair debate what to do with the human race.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:34.780
SCP-4568-1 was not difficult to discover once
it started moving.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:38.550
In fact, it was almost impossible to ignore.

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:42.770
Earthquakes have been tearing across South
America for centuries, destroying homes, taking

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:48.439
the lives of innocent people, and fundamentally
changing the shape of our planet itself.

00:03:48.439 --> 00:03:52.110
What most people do not realize, however,
is that the fault line running through the

00:03:52.110 --> 00:03:56.480
Andes mountain range has actually largely
been dormant during this period.

00:03:56.480 --> 00:04:01.409
The source of the earthquakes has come from
something far more mysterious.

00:04:01.409 --> 00:04:06.519
Our innocent hiker, Diego, had been spending
the week walking among the Andes when the

00:04:06.519 --> 00:04:08.000
earthquake struck.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:13.000
You would be forgiven for assuming, as Diego
did, that the ground rising beneath his feet

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:17.600
was a new mountain forming as the tectonic
plates crashed together.

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:22.109
But the staggering reality of the situation
was that he found himself hiking along the

00:04:22.109 --> 00:04:26.410
back of SCP-4568-1.

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:31.570
As the creature raised its head into the air,
Diego saw the head of a serpent lifting several

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:33.509
kilometers away from him.

00:04:33.509 --> 00:04:38.229
Its body stretched and wound its way through
the mountain range, filling the valleys and

00:04:38.229 --> 00:04:40.450
running beneath his feet.

00:04:40.450 --> 00:04:45.199
The scale of SCP-4568-1 is hard to convey.

00:04:45.199 --> 00:04:51.051
Measuring over 500 kilometers in length, this
serpent is longer than most US states, with

00:04:51.051 --> 00:04:53.379
a 20 km width.

00:04:53.379 --> 00:04:57.759
Standing on the back of it quite literally
feels like standing on a mountain range.

00:04:57.759 --> 00:05:03.639
For context, the horizon at sea level is about
4.8 kilometers away, so multiply that by 4,

00:05:03.639 --> 00:05:07.370
and you’ll get a sense of just how wide
this thing is.

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:12.290
Even small movements from this SCP are enough
to trigger continent-wide earthquakes, with

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:15.570
tremors being felt all the way around the
world.

00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:20.419
Upon the initial discovery of this SCP, the
Foundation was unable to determine why it

00:05:20.419 --> 00:05:26.400
remains dormant for such long periods and
seems to only awaken sporadically and for

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:28.259
brief periods of time.

00:05:28.259 --> 00:05:33.319
That was, until SCP-4568-2 was discovered.

00:05:33.319 --> 00:05:37.490
It is little wonder that the second serpent
took so long to be found.

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:42.180
Its body is composed almost entirely of water,
sand, algae, and steam.

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:47.620
It does not show up on sonar scans and is
incredibly difficult to detect in the water,

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:48.940
even visually.

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:51.750
Its form is loosely defined whilst dormant.

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:59.240
With broadly similar measurements to SCP-4568-1,
this serpent roams the South Pacific Ocean.

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:04.440
Any marine creatures that swim into the SCP's
body find themselves undergoing beneficial

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:05.890
mutations.

00:06:05.890 --> 00:06:11.690
Crabs grow extra pincers, bottom feeders grow
larger mouths, and sharks find themselves

00:06:11.690 --> 00:06:15.880
developing heightened senses and even extra
hearts.

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:22.699
These marine animals seem to undergo virtually
no distress and are free to exit and re-enter

00:06:22.699 --> 00:06:26.010
the SCP's body at any point.

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:30.460
Initially, SCP-4568-2 was believed to be the
peaceful one of the pair.

00:06:30.460 --> 00:06:33.880
Both serpents seemed to become active at the
same time.

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:40.880
While on land, SCP-4568-1 would wreak havoc
with magnitude 7 earthquakes in major metropolitan

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:45.970
areas, the sea serpent's function was less
well understood.

00:06:45.970 --> 00:06:51.139
Employing resonant frequencies and vibrations,
this SCP was able to give its watery body

00:06:51.139 --> 00:06:55.910
a distinct form as it rose up from the ocean
and towered above the waves.

00:06:55.910 --> 00:07:01.599
In order to maintain its shape and control
its movements, this SCP employed a huge amount

00:07:01.599 --> 00:07:02.599
of energy.

00:07:02.599 --> 00:07:07.340
However, the Foundation quickly observed that
it was rarely able to maintain its form for

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:08.690
very long.

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:13.669
As soon as the sea serpent rose out of the
water, its mountainous twin would begin to

00:07:13.669 --> 00:07:20.139
move, sending tremors around the world that
disrupted the frequency needed for SCP-4568-2

00:07:20.139 --> 00:07:21.720
to remain animate.

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:26.879
Exhausted and unable to maintain its shape,
the sea serpent would fall into another period

00:07:26.879 --> 00:07:31.000
of dormancy, gliding lazily through the oceans.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:33.830
But this dormancy suited the Foundation.

00:07:33.830 --> 00:07:38.220
Without the constant seismic tremors, researchers
could work fast.

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:41.720
Two operating bases were set up to monitor
each SCP.

00:07:41.720 --> 00:07:47.379
Two mirrored bases with mirrored teams in
constant communication with one another.

00:07:47.379 --> 00:07:52.620
As soon as one team made a discovery, it was
conveyed to the others and vice versa.

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:56.860
One operating base was set up high in the
Andes mountains, specifically designed to

00:07:56.860 --> 00:08:03.229
be as earthquake-proof as possible, capable
of withstanding earthquakes of up to 9.9 magnitude.

00:08:03.229 --> 00:08:08.090
Meanwhile, in the South Pacific Ocean, an
underwater research center was built just

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:13.449
above the seabed, with regular vessels drifting
out into the unknown to gather whatever data

00:08:13.449 --> 00:08:16.710
they could about the great SCPs.

00:08:16.710 --> 00:08:19.040
Several early findings stood out.

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:25.419
Firstly, SCP-4568-1 appeared to have a very
different internal structure from its twin.

00:08:25.419 --> 00:08:29.479
Researchers initially assumed that the creature
would be largely composed of earth minerals

00:08:29.479 --> 00:08:33.229
and rock, as its exterior appearance suggested.

00:08:33.229 --> 00:08:38.510
However, scans of its body indicated the presence
of what can only be assumed to be artificially

00:08:38.510 --> 00:08:40.599
created components.

00:08:40.599 --> 00:08:46.190
Great gears resembling clockwork structures
and even rudimentary circuitry were present

00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:47.970
throughout the creature's body.

00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:52.640
The function or origin of these gears has
yet to be determined, especially as there

00:08:52.640 --> 00:08:58.311
is no evident way that their movement corresponds
to the autonomy and movement of the serpent

00:08:58.311 --> 00:08:59.710
itself.

00:08:59.710 --> 00:09:04.050
The far more striking discovery, however,
came when the SCP Foundation discovered a

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:06.990
way to communicate with the two beasts.

00:09:06.990 --> 00:09:12.550
Ultra-low-frequency waves capable of traveling
vast distances, even light years, were discovered

00:09:12.550 --> 00:09:17.010
to be emitted from the two serpents' heads
at intermittent periods.

00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:21.440
The Foundation had to develop some of the
largest antennas ever created to pick up these

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:25.430
frequencies and interpret the data coming
through them.

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:30.510
What they found were two twins locked in a
fierce debate about the fate of humanity and

00:09:30.510 --> 00:09:31.870
the universe itself.

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:37.490
It was only then that the motivations of these
two serpents started to make sense.

00:09:37.490 --> 00:09:42.820
In 2010, almost as soon as the Foundation
was able to tap into the frequency, they were

00:09:42.820 --> 00:09:45.570
contacted directly by SCP-4568-1.

00:09:45.570 --> 00:09:51.010
"Fundacion, I know you can now hear me.

00:09:51.010 --> 00:09:53.360
I will not apologize for my actions.

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:59.060
I know that I am the reason that millions
of your kind face their demise.

00:09:59.060 --> 00:10:03.220
I know your pain and I feel it too.

00:10:03.220 --> 00:10:05.850
But I shall never apologize for it.

00:10:05.850 --> 00:10:12.310
I simply ask you to listen to myself and to
my [word cannot be translated].

00:10:12.310 --> 00:10:15.880
You are curious, you can be patient.

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:20.459
Exercise that and you may one day understand."

00:10:20.459 --> 00:10:21.951
And listen, the Foundation did.

00:10:21.951 --> 00:10:26.910
Efforts to contain or destroy the two serpents
were put on the back burner.

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:32.360
Instead, Foundation agents prioritized spreading
disinformation across South America and beyond

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:34.899
about the source of these earthquakes.

00:10:34.899 --> 00:10:40.269
The two serpents are far too large and far
too powerful to overcome or contain.

00:10:40.269 --> 00:10:45.350
Instead, the Foundation prioritized the use
of amnestic drugs, disinformation, and the

00:10:45.350 --> 00:10:51.300
creation of fringe conspiracy groups to discredit
any claims of the serpents' respective existences.

00:10:51.300 --> 00:10:56.540
Meanwhile, some of the most senior leadership
figures in the Foundation were and still are

00:10:56.540 --> 00:11:01.250
locked in a fierce debate as to what to do
with the twin serpents.

00:11:01.250 --> 00:11:07.690
By listening to the communications between
the two SCPs, the Foundation discovered that

00:11:07.690 --> 00:11:12.670
SCP-4568-2 is intent on wiping out the entire
human race.

00:11:12.670 --> 00:11:17.320
The only thing that has prevented it from
being able to do so thus far has been the

00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:20.320
existence of the other serpent.

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:27.250
Every time that SCP-4568-2 begins to mount
an attack on humanity, its land-bearing twin

00:11:27.250 --> 00:11:30.730
triggers enormous earthquakes to disrupt its
progress.

00:11:30.730 --> 00:11:35.250
But why would the sea serpent want to destroy
the human race?

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:41.990
As Foundation generals gathered in the deep
sea operations base, SCP-4568-2 came to the

00:11:41.990 --> 00:11:46.010
observation window to look them in the eyes
as it told them:

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:49.270
"I am sure you can see it.

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:53.820
How your world dies a little bit more every
day.

00:11:53.820 --> 00:11:56.290
Mostly by your own hand, no?

00:11:56.290 --> 00:12:00.570
You poison the oceans, taint the rivers, blacken
the skies.

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:05.600
You do not need angels of death to destroy
your world.

00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:07.960
But there is something else.

00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:13.000
I see it, in the bottom of your eyes: something
unforgettable.

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:19.390
Unconceivable ideas, cloaked in madness and
impossible colors.

00:12:19.390 --> 00:12:24.980
Do you think I will let you drag the rest
of the world down with yourselves?

00:12:24.980 --> 00:12:33.100
Do you think I will leave this world, my world,
to die in flames?

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:38.450
It sees your world, and it comes in fives."

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:42.940
Since this revelation, the Foundation has
poured countless hours and resources into

00:12:42.940 --> 00:12:45.589
trying to identify a cosmic threat.

00:12:45.589 --> 00:12:50.209
For well over a decade, many of the smartest
scientists the world has to offer have looked

00:12:50.209 --> 00:12:57.730
to the night sky, scanning for this impossible
color, this shroud of madness, but to no avail.

00:12:57.730 --> 00:13:02.620
Some within the Foundation believe the Serpent
is lying, trying to make up an excuse to justify

00:13:02.620 --> 00:13:10.690
its genocide, but information from SCP-4568-1
seems to confirm everyone's worst fears.

00:13:10.690 --> 00:13:13.160
"Your minds burn bright, Fundacion.

00:13:13.160 --> 00:13:19.440
All of humanity shines from this rock like
a candle in a dark room.

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:20.670
It sees you.

00:13:20.670 --> 00:13:25.600
An idea exists only because something thought
of it.

00:13:25.600 --> 00:13:30.850
Have you even considered how such terrible
concepts could have been given form?

00:13:30.850 --> 00:13:34.740
What kind of atrocious mind could even think
about it?

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:38.180
Humans cannot conceive the colorless green.

00:13:38.180 --> 00:13:42.699
What if you are playing into this creature's
hands?"

00:13:42.699 --> 00:13:48.390
There appears to be an underlying implication
that ideas are the source of power somehow.

00:13:48.390 --> 00:13:56.259
This colorless green, this unimaginable cosmic
threat, seems to be a monstrous idea incarnate.

00:13:56.259 --> 00:13:57.920
But whose idea?

00:13:57.920 --> 00:13:58.920
Humanity’s?

00:13:58.920 --> 00:14:03.870
There is a deep lore that the two serpents
discuss with one another, one that makes little

00:14:03.870 --> 00:14:06.760
sense even to this day to the Foundation.

00:14:06.760 --> 00:14:14.040
They talk of gods and goddesses, deities of
flesh, of steel and gears, and of ‘the fives’.

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:18.510
Quite what these creatures are, if they are
even creatures at all, is a mystery to the

00:14:18.510 --> 00:14:20.370
Foundation.

00:14:20.370 --> 00:14:24.889
Researchers have not discovered a way of communicating
back with the two serpents directly.

00:14:24.889 --> 00:14:30.420
Attempts to mimic their language or transmit
signals asking questions to them have been

00:14:30.420 --> 00:14:31.810
largely ignored.

00:14:31.810 --> 00:14:37.130
Instead, they address humanity and the Foundation
as a whole, seeming to take the view of the

00:14:37.130 --> 00:14:43.800
human race as being a collective hive of mind,
one that they are evidently able to tap into.

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:49.759
The pair seem uninterested in informing us
as to exactly what this threat is or explaining

00:14:49.759 --> 00:14:51.820
who the gods and goddesses are.

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:57.570
Perhaps they assume we know these things already,
or more likely, they believe that our consciousness

00:14:57.570 --> 00:15:03.190
is not yet capable of perceiving the scale
and depth of the concepts they are debating.

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:09.019
What is clear, however, is their shared understanding
that if humanity were to be eliminated, the

00:15:09.019 --> 00:15:14.430
candle was to be blown out, this cosmic threat
would pass by.

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:15.900
The pair have names.

00:15:15.900 --> 00:15:20.910
Trentrén is the land serpent, while remaining
dormant much of the time in an enormous cave

00:15:20.910 --> 00:15:23.329
system beneath the Andes Mountains.

00:15:23.329 --> 00:15:27.190
This serpent seems keen to help the Foundation
in some way.

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:33.430
Kaikai, the sea serpent, is intent on sacrificing
the human race for a greater good, one far

00:15:33.430 --> 00:15:36.009
beyond our understanding.

00:15:36.009 --> 00:15:40.810
Speaking to the Foundation in the Andes Mountains,
Trentrén gave a short speech that served

00:15:40.810 --> 00:15:45.110
both as encouragement and a terrible warning
of the darkness to come.

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:48.860
"It is something I like about you, Fundación.

00:15:48.860 --> 00:15:49.860
About mankind.

00:15:49.860 --> 00:15:56.709
While it is easy to just take the simplest
path, to just give up, there will always be

00:15:56.709 --> 00:16:02.279
some among you who refuse this path, who do
the right thing.

00:16:02.279 --> 00:16:08.639
Maybe not all of you are this strong, but
I can see it in your methods, those so-called

00:16:08.639 --> 00:16:10.740
'containment procedures.'

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:16.500
There will always be someone who stands up
against the dark, even if it takes a thousand

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:20.089
million years to emerge victorious.

00:16:20.089 --> 00:16:24.420
Maybe you can stop the Fifth.

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:27.699
After all, ideas can be killed with better
ideas."

00:16:27.699 --> 00:16:32.290
Even if it takes a thousand million years…

00:16:32.290 --> 00:16:38.790
Now go check out “SCP-2317 - The Devourer
of Worlds / A Door to Another World” and

00:16:38.790 --> 00:16:40.230
“SCP-001 - The World's Gone Beautiful!”

